{
  "slug": "docker-and-kubernetes-devkit",
  "name": "Docker And Kubernetes Devkit",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Generate Dockerfiles and Kubernetes manifests, debug failing containers and pods, and audit Helm charts and RBAC. Opinionated, safety-conscious workflows for Docker and Kubernetes from local builds through production clusters.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **7 skills**, **3 agents**, **5 commands** and **2 hooks**.\n\n- **Skills** (7): `compose` (Generate or update a docker-compose.yml file for a multi-service local development setup), `docker-debug` (Diagnose why a Docker build is failing or why a container will not start or is crashing), `dockerfile` (Generate a production-grade Dockerfile for the current project), `helm-review` (Review a Helm chart for security issues, correctness, and production readiness), `k8s-debug` (Investigate a failing Kubernetes pod or workload by pulling events, logs, and describe output), `manifest` (Generate Kubernetes manifests from a plain-English description of what to deploy), `rbac-review` (Audit Kubernetes RBAC for overly broad permissions)\n- **Agents** (3): `container-forensics` (Use when a Docker build or container is failing and the user needs a root-cause diagnosis), `manifest-author` (Use when writing, restructuring, or reviewing Kubernetes manifests (Deployment, Service, Ingress, ConfigMap, Secret, HPA, PDB, StatefulSet, DaemonSet, Job,…), `pod-forensics` (Use when a Kubernetes pod is in a bad state (CrashLoopBackOff, ImagePullBackOff, OOMKilled, Pending, Init:Error, Running but not…)\n- **Commands** (5): `cluster-audit` (Run the full Docker and Kubernetes audit pass in one command), `doctor` (Check the local Docker and Kubernetes toolchain), `events` (Watch Kubernetes events sorted by timestamp, with optional namespace and type filters), `runtime-check` (Check which local Docker, Compose, Kubernetes, Helm, WSL, and alternative container runtimes are available), `smoke-test` (Run a live local smoke test for the plugin's Docker, Compose, Helm, and kubectl workflows)\n- **Hooks** (2): `SessionStart`, `PostToolUse`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install docker-and-kubernetes-devkit@claude-community` from `mohitkale/docker-kubernetes`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
